# This working tree is used from both Windows and WSL against the same files
# (/mnt/c/...), so line endings must be LF on disk, not "native".
#
# `* text=auto` alone normalises to LF *in the repository* but checks out CRLF
# on Windows, which makes every shell script fail under WSL bash with
#   run.sh: line 30: $'\r': command not found
# because the \r becomes part of the command. Pinning eol=lf keeps the working
# tree LF on every platform.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.npy   binary
*.pth   binary
*.tar   binary
*.gz    binary
